(7505763, 1196727, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>An interesting idea Fabio, generally well executed. I have to agree with your commenter I do think the image would be improved with a plainer background. The idea and the figure is cute, it makes the viewer smile which has to be a good thing. The shallow DOF at maximum aperture works well with sufficient detail where it is needed. The composition is good with some effective cropping and a nice diagonal it raises it to a higher standard its just a shame that the brightly coloured background feels somewhat at odds with the content.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge An interesting idea Fabio, generally well executed. I have to agree with your commenter I do think the image would be improved with a plainer background. The idea and the figure is cute, it makes the viewer smile which has to be a good thing. The shallow DOF at maximum aperture works well with sufficient detail where it is needed. The composition is good with some effective cropping and a nice diagonal it raises it to a higher standard its just a shame that the brightly coloured background feels somewhat at odds with the content.', '2017-03-20 09:45:02.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505764, 1196513, 25024, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club<br/> <br/>An appealing image that meets the challenge<br/> <br/>Nice idea Marcel. The image is well executed with a nice shallow and appropriate DOF, the earphones work well against the music manuscript. I like the diagonal you have positioned the music on it adds a dynamic to the overall result. The mono processing works well and is again most appropriate for the image. A good image whose musical message is never in doubt, well done.</td>', 'Hello from the critique club An appealing image that meets the challenge Nice idea Marcel. The image is well executed with a nice shallow and appropriate DOF, the earphones work well against the music manuscript. I like the diagonal you have positioned the music on it adds a dynamic to the overall result. The mono processing works well and is again most appropriate for the image. A good image whose musical message is never in doubt, well done.', '2017-03-20 09:49:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505766, 1196749, 118154, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by skewsme:</b></div><hr/><i>  I am glad I don''t have to wear her shoes!  :-) </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>me too</td>', 'Originally posted by skewsme:  I am glad I don''t have to wear her shoes!  :-)   me too', '2017-03-20 10:12:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505773, 1196537, 19825, '<td valign="top">This is very nice -- good composition and processing. I cannot figure out how anyone could have given this a 2 (or even a 4 or 5). Congrats on the Top 5 finish and new personal best.</td>', 'This is very nice -- good composition and processing. I cannot figure out how anyone could have given this a 2 (or even a 4 or 5). Congrats on the Top 5 finish and new personal best.', '2017-03-20 11:42:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505774, 1196275, 19825, '<td valign="top">This is excellent, Lydia. For what it''s worth -- While three arms would come in "handy" (except when shopping for shirts, coats, etc), you might consider using the Transform feature of PS. I generally use it in the RAW processor -- draw a "horizontal" lines along the table top and horn and a vertical on the mic, and, presto, PS squares everything up.</td>', 'This is excellent, Lydia. For what it''s worth -- While three arms would come in "handy" (except when shopping for shirts, coats, etc), you might consider using the Transform feature of PS. I generally use it in the RAW processor -- draw a "horizontal" lines along the table top and horn and a vertical on the mic, and, presto, PS squares everything up.', '2017-03-20 11:53:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(7505775, 1196537, 167587, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by markwiley:</b></div><hr/><i> This is very nice -- good composition and processing. I cannot figure out how anyone could have given this a 2 (or even a 4 or 5). Congrats on the Top 5 finish and new personal best. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Thanks for the kind words and the compliments. Everybody has different tastes!</td>', 'Originally posted by markwiley: This is very nice -- good composition and processing. I cannot figure out how anyone could have given this a 2 (or even a 4 or 5). Congrats on the Top 5 finish and new personal best.   Thanks for the kind words and the compliments. Everybody has different tastes!', '2017-03-20 12:09:10.000000', NULL, 0),
